  "description": "FAFQAF01 crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C25 H79 Er4 N5 O24 8+,8(Cl1 1-),12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.686-3.819 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.34-109.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4(μ3-OH)4(Val)5(H2O)10]8+. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 8+.",
